<title>ITALY: Italian lira firms past new ERM central parity.</title>
<headline>Italian lira firms past new ERM central parity.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian lira strengthened past its new central parity of 990.00 per mark in Europe's exchange rate mechanism (ERM) to trade at 989.80, traders said.</p>
<p>The lira, which was readmitted on Sunday to the ERM after four years outside, was quoted at 990.00/0.40 per mark moments after going through the level.  </p>
<p>The lira last traded at a stronger level than 990.00 on October 7 this year when it touched 988.40. Before that however it had not trade as such a firm level since July 1994.</p>
</text>
